// §14 entry 13 -- non-atomic `refero` crossing an `externus` boundary ->
// EXS-E0520.
//
// §6.4: "`refero<T>` -- non-atomic. Cannot cross `externus` (EXS-E0520). A
// foreign thread racing a non-atomic refcount is a use-after-free, and the
// type system cannot see the escape." §5.3 gives the `externus` block
// syntax this fixture reuses directly. `refero_communis<T>` (atomic) is the
// type that MAY cross this same boundary -- its absence here is the point,
// not an oversight.
//
// RUNS since 6f6cd8c (2026-09-25). The EXS-E0520 rule existed and was
// unit-pinned from a hand-built AST (tests/unit/chk_ty_e0520_refero.asm)
// because `refero` was a reserved word with no phrase-level form: this
// file was EXS-E0201 at the word. 6f6cd8c gives spec 8.6's CoreType the
// alternative `'refero' GenericArgs` (one peek, `refero <`), and the
// from-source twin tests/unit/chk_ty_e0520_refero_source.asm pins that
// `refero<u32>` is E0520 and `refero_communis<u32>` is silent. This
// fixture needed no edit. Measured on the main tree at fe24fe5: exactly
// {EXS-E0520}, exit 1.

structura Nodus { valor: mensura }

externus("C", abi: sysv_amd64) {
    functio consume_nodum(n: refero<Nodus>) -> mensura
}

